MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The fender washers and M6 bolts felt like useful additions to my existing bolt and rivet nut kits: the washers spread mounting loads, while the bolts offer lengths I could use with threaded inserts.",
    "The magnetic hooks fit my interest in practical mounting supplies, and the pegboard recognized a plausible need to organize my growing collection of tools."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Crucible tongs and electrical test leads require specific tasks I have not shown a need for; buying fabrication tools does not mean I am melting metal or testing electrical circuits.",
    "Gaffers tape does not serve the same immediate purpose as my adhesive mounting supplies, and calibration weights do not follow from using calipers or a temperature gun."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seemed to treat workshop equipment as broadly interchangeable, even though I choose tools for particular fastening, mounting, and fabrication jobs.",
    "Some suggestions relied too much on shared words or general functions: tape for mounting led to backdrop tape, and measurement tools led to scale calibration supplies."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Compatibility and added usefulness matter: washers and additional M6 lengths can complement what I own, while another small metric screw assortment largely repeats supplies I already have.",
    "An item can fit my interests without being a purchase I would make now. Casters need a specific bench, and pegboard needs suitable capacity and mounting options before I would choose it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my fastening and mounting interests, but sometimes stretched them into unrelated workshop tasks or overlooked what would add useful capability now."
}
